  "draft_notes_entry": "## x5 \u2014 the battery-genericity of the one-T fit: BATTERY-SPECIFIC (the proper full-logit adjudication of T229's registered prediction; x4's desk attempt was honestly instrument-limited \u2014 the bracket bound inverts past the p=0.5 crossings) (2026-10-04T21:51:55Z) \u2014 DONE\n\nWHAT WE DID: re-probed the committed two-wash states ONCE with full answer-position logit dumps for the ctrl battery (n=12) and near (n=3, co-report) \u2014 the e238 dump conventions verbatim, every state re-probe-certified against e214's committed records (max dp 0.00e+00, tol 0.005; vs e238's own npz: max|dlogit| 0.0, bit-identical) \u2014 then the committed MLE one-T fit per state per battery (TempFamily verbatim) against e238's committed fact-side curve.\n\nWHAT WE SAW: ctrl's T diverges from the committed fact-side curve (= fact's, the pooled-54 reference) by > 0.15 at 4 adjudication states (deltas: w1+10 -0.0167, w1+50 -0.1654, w1+80 -0.1876, w2+10 -0.0188, w2+50 -0.1579, w2+80 -0.1665) OR ctrl's own-fit R2 left [0.2, 0.6] at: w1+80 +0.6324, w2+10 +0.6095 (all six: w1+10 +0.5159, w1+50 +0.5339, w1+80 +0.6324, w2+10 +0.6095, w2+50 +0.5257, w2+80 +0.5961) \u2014 the batteries have different thermal signatures; x4's +10 signal read at full precision: x4's +10 slice said ctrl flattens MORE than fact (bracket medians ctrl 1.28-1.33 vs fact 0.96-0.99, gaps w1+10: +0.32, w2+10: +0.34). At full precision the ctrl-fact gaps are w1+10: +0.0225, w2+10: +0.0208 \u2014 the bracket's DIRECTION (ctrl > fact) is CONFIRMED, but its MAGNITUDE was instrument-artifact: the bracket's ~+0.3 gap reads as ~+0.02 under the full-logit family. Against the committed pooled reference, ctrl sits BELOW it at +10 (w1+10: -0.0167, w2+10: -0.0188). The ORDERING at the deep states is stable across washes: ctrl LOW (1.18-1.27) < fact-only (1.26-1.37) < the committed pooled curve (1.34-1.45) < near (1.42-1.63) < tmpl (1.51-1.65) \u2014 every battery its own T(t); near's deltas vs the committed curve: w1+10 +0.072, w1+50 +0.131, w1+80 +0.176, w2+10 +0.085, w2+50 +0.087, w2+80 +0.077 (its +-0.12 clause also fails at w1+80). THE t0 ANCHOR read 1.0000 (the instrument's positive control).\n\nHONESTY: n=1 organism; near n=3 (coarse); the reference curve is the pooled-54 fit and contains ctrl (self-reference disclosed; the fact-only co-report tracks it within 0.100; ctrl-vs-fact-only deltas stay inside +0.13, so the R2 clause carries the verdict under either reference \u2014 disclosed sensitivity, not a re-adjudication); lens-not-mechanism (T228/T229); wash-1 CPU replay vs wash-2 GPU (the archive's asymmetry, inherited)."
